    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes, as printed. If $|x|=k$, then $k\\geq0$ and $x=k$ or $x=-k$. A negative $k$ cannot satisfy the premise.",
      "worked": "Suppose $|x|=k$. If $x\\geq0$, then $|x|=x$, so $x=k$. If $x<0$, then $|x|=-x$, so $x=-k$. Thus the printed implication is true.\n\nFor $k<0$, the equation $|x|=k$ has no real solution. Such a value does not provide a counterexample to an implication whose premise is $|x|=k$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
